      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Shallan Davar followed Jasnah Kholin from city to city asking to be her ward. Impressed that Shallan had taught herself and kept on studying, Jasnah accepted her.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "8" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Litima brought her single ward with her when she read from The Way of Kings to Dalinar.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "26" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Navani Kholin had no wards of her own but sometimes borrowed them from other lighteyes in the warcamps.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Teshav Khal kept many wards, two of them senior, and at least one went with her as she carried out her duties.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "18" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "81" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "44" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Karavangia, granddaughter of King Taravangian, became the ward of a scholar soon after her grandfather became king of Jah Keved.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Many women sought to be Jasnah's ward, twelve in 1173 alone, and Shallan was the only one she took. The wardship went on after Shallan became a Lightweaver and ended some eight months after she married Adolin.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "8" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "44" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "21" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Kalami had several wards with her when the Sibling sent Navani a spanreed message that the tower was under attack.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "39" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Neshan and both of Neshan's wards were killed early in the invasion of Urithiru.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "46" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
